# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: description
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a learning experiment for the latest version of Qiskit noise learning"
msgstr "Costruisci un esperimento di apprendimento per l'ultima versione di Qiskit noise learning"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a learning experiment"
msgstr "Costruire un esperimento di apprendimento"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a learning experiment {#build-a-learning-experiment}"
msgstr "Costruire un esperimento di apprendimento {#build-a-learning-experiment}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial demonstrates how to build a standard learning experiment from scratch, and use it to learn a model from simulated noisy data.\n"
msgstr "Questo tutorial mostra come costruire da zero un esperimento di apprendimento standard e usarlo per apprendere un modello da dati rumorosi simulati.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '1.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define a gate set on a ring of qubits\n"
msgstr "Definire un gate set su un anello di qubit\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '2.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choose a 2-local Pauli-Lindblad model\n"
msgstr "Scegliere un modello di Pauli-Lindblad 2-locale\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '3.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build the learning experiment\n"
msgstr "Costruire l'esperimento di apprendimento\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '4.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generate circuits\n"
msgstr "Generare i circuiti\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '5.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Set up local simulation\n"
msgstr "Configurare la simulazione locale\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '6.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the program\n"
msgstr "Eseguire il programma\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '7.  '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Analyze the data\n"
msgstr "Analizzare i dati\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition title=\"Running on real hardware\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  The circuits below are simulated locally, so this walkthrough needs no IBM Quantum® credentials. To alternatively run it on a real device:\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition title=\"Esecuzione su hardware reale\" type=\"note\">\n"
"  I circuiti seguenti sono simulati localmente, quindi questa guida non richiede credenziali IBM Quantum®. Per eseguirla invece su un dispositivo reale:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Bullet: '  *   '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Step 1**: replace [`FakeMarrakesh`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-provider-fake-marrakesh \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") with a real backend.\n"
msgstr "**Passo 1**: sostituisci [`FakeMarrakesh`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-provider-fake-marrakesh \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") con un backend reale.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  *   **Step 5**: pass that backend as the executor’s mode, and drop the simulator options.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"  *   **Passo 5**: passa quel backend come modalità dell'executor e rimuovi le opzioni del simulatore.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"define-a-gate-set-on-a-ring-of-qubits\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Define a gate set on a ring of qubits {#1-define-a-gate-set-on-a-ring-of-qubits}"
msgstr "1. Definire un gate set su un anello di qubit {#1-define-a-gate-set-on-a-ring-of-qubits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build a [`QiskitGateSet`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/gate-sets-qiskit-gate-set#qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGateSet \"qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGateSet\") from a backend [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) and a subset of its qubits — here a twelve-qubit ring of [`FakeMarrakesh`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-provider-fake-marrakesh \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") — then add one gate to it: a layer of six `CZ` gates covering that ring. By default the gate set is initialized with a preparation gate `P` and a measurement gate `M`.\n"
msgstr "Costruisci un [`QiskitGateSet`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/gate-sets-qiskit-gate-set#qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGateSet \"qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGateSet\") a partire da un [`Target`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.transpiler.Target) di un backend e da un sottoinsieme dei suoi qubit — qui un anello di dodici qubit di [`FakeMarrakesh`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/fake-provider-fake-marrakesh \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") — quindi aggiungi un gate: un layer di sei gate `CZ` che copre quell'anello. Per impostazione predefinita il gate set viene inizializzato con un gate di preparazione `P` e un gate di misura `M`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Running on real hardware\">\n"
msgstr "<DoqAdmonition type=\"note\" title=\"Esecuzione su hardware reale\">\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "</DoqAdmonition>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Call [`draw()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/gate-sets-gate-set#qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.GateSet.draw \"qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.GateSet.draw\") to see the gate on the device topology: the ring of qubits in the gate set, and which pairs of them the gate entangles.\n"
msgstr "Chiama [`draw()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/gate-sets-gate-set#qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.GateSet.draw \"qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.GateSet.draw\") per vedere il gate sulla topologia del dispositivo: l'anello di qubit nel gate set e quali coppie di essi il gate entangla.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"choose-a-2-local-pauli-lindblad-model\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Choose a 2-local Pauli-Lindblad model {#2-choose-a-2-local-pauli-lindblad-model}"
msgstr "2. Scegliere un modello di Pauli-Lindblad 2-locale {#2-choose-a-2-local-pauli-lindblad-model}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Decide which Pauli-Lindblad generators the noise is allowed to have with a [`PauliLindbladModel`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/models-pauli-lindblad-model#qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel \"qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel\"). Build that generator set from the gate set’s connectivity with [`k_local()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/models-pauli-lindblad-model#qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel.k_local \"qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel.k_local\") — here every 2-local Pauli on connected qubit pairs of the unitary gate, and single-qubit Paulis for preparation and measurement.\n"
msgstr "Decidi quali generatori di Pauli-Lindblad può avere il rumore con un [`PauliLindbladModel`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/models-pauli-lindblad-model#qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel \"qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel\"). Costruisci quell'insieme di generatori dalla connettività del gate set con [`k_local()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/models-pauli-lindblad-model#qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel.k_local \"qiskit_noise_learning.models.PauliLindbladModel.k_local\") — qui ogni Pauli 2-locale sulle coppie di qubit connessi del gate unitario e i Pauli a singolo qubit per preparazione e misura.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Display the unknown parameter count for the noise model of each gate.\n"
msgstr "Mostra il numero di parametri incogniti del modello di rumore di ogni gate.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"build-the-learning-experiment\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Build the learning experiment {#3-build-the-learning-experiment}"
msgstr "3. Costruire l'esperimento di apprendimento {#3-build-the-learning-experiment}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Assemble an [`Experiment`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/experiment-builder-experiment#qiskit_noise_learning.experiment_builder.Experiment \"qiskit_noise_learning.experiment_builder.Experiment\") by composing builder stages. Each stage reads what earlier stages wrote, so order matters:\n"
msgstr "Assembla un [`Experiment`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/experiment-builder-experiment#qiskit_noise_learning.experiment_builder.Experiment \"qiskit_noise_learning.experiment_builder.Experiment\") componendo gli stadi del builder. Ogni stadio legge ciò che hanno scritto gli stadi precedenti, quindi l'ordine conta:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Observe design matrix rank:\n"
msgstr "Osserva il rango della matrice di progetto:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"generate-circuits\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Generate circuits {#4-generate-circuits}"
msgstr "4. Generare i circuiti {#4-generate-circuits}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compile the experiment with an [`ExecutorCircuitGenerator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/circuit-generator-executor-circuit-generator#qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator \"qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator\"), generating a [`QuantumProgram`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/quantum-program-quantum-program \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") — one parameterized template circuit per fragment depth.\n"
msgstr "Compila l'esperimento con un [`ExecutorCircuitGenerator`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/circuit-generator-executor-circuit-generator#qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator \"qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator\"), generando un [`QuantumProgram`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/quantum-program-quantum-program \"(in Qiskit Runtime IBM Client)\") — un circuito template parametrizzato per ogni profondità di frammento.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Draw a template circuit to inspect.\n"
msgstr "Disegna un circuito template da ispezionare.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![../\\_images/4088c7e98baeb5b56925c6c1f276159582c5f7040fbba76de438b919210bcc5f.png](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-noise-learning/4088c7e98baeb5b56925c6c1f276159582c5f7040fbba76de438b919210bcc5f.avif)\n"
msgstr "![../\\_images/4088c7e98baeb5b56925c6c1f276159582c5f7040fbba76de438b919210bcc5f.png](/docs/images/addons/qiskit-noise-learning/4088c7e98baeb5b56925c6c1f276159582c5f7040fbba76de438b919210bcc5f.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"set-up-local-simulation\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Set up local simulation {#5-set-up-local-simulation}"
msgstr "5. Configurare la simulazione locale {#5-set-up-local-simulation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To define the noise model for simulation, we use the generators already in the model with random rates to construct a [`PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap).\n"
msgstr "Per definire il modello di rumore per la simulazione, usiamo i generatori già presenti nel modello con tassi casuali per costruire una [`PauliLindbladMap`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Those maps are as wide as the device, since the model is expressed in `backend`’s qubit indexing, but the simulator wants each map to be as wide as the gate it applies to, with Pauli indices running over the gate’s qubits in ascending physical order. Narrow them with [`keep_qubits()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap#keep_qubits), which traces out everything off the ring:\n"
msgstr "Quelle mappe sono ampie quanto il dispositivo, poiché il modello è espresso nell'indicizzazione dei qubit di `backend`, ma il simulatore richiede che ogni mappa sia ampia quanto il gate a cui si applica, con gli indici di Pauli che scorrono sui qubit del gate in ordine fisico crescente. Restringile con [`keep_qubits()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.PauliLindbladMap#keep_qubits), che traccia via tutto ciò che sta fuori dall'anello:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The simulator names a layer’s noise by the box instruction the layer was built from, which [`to_instruction()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/gate-sets-qiskit-gate#qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGate.to_instruction \"qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGate.to_instruction\") returns for any gate in the gate set. Pair each box with its map, use the stabilizer simulation method, and set `seed_simulator` to make the simulated data reproducible:\n"
msgstr "Il simulatore assegna un nome al rumore di un layer in base all'istruzione box da cui il layer è stato costruito, che [`to_instruction()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/gate-sets-qiskit-gate#qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGate.to_instruction \"qiskit_noise_learning.gate_sets.QiskitGate.to_instruction\") restituisce per qualsiasi gate del gate set. Associa ogni box alla sua mappa, usa il metodo di simulazione stabilizer e imposta `seed_simulator` per rendere riproducibili i dati simulati:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"run-the-program\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Run the program {#6-run-the-program}"
msgstr "6. Eseguire il programma {#6-run-the-program}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Run the program, then format the results with [`collect()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/circuit-generator-executor-circuit-generator#qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator.collect \"qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator.collect\"), to produce a [`Fit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/analysis-fit#qiskit_noise_learning.analysis.Fit \"qiskit_noise_learning.analysis.Fit\") — the container the analysis stages read from and write to.\n"
msgstr "Esegui il programma, quindi formatta i risultati con [`collect()`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/circuit-generator-executor-circuit-generator#qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator.collect \"qiskit_noise_learning.circuit_generator.ExecutorCircuitGenerator.collect\"), per produrre un [`Fit`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-noise-learning/generated/analysis-fit#qiskit_noise_learning.analysis.Fit \"qiskit_noise_learning.analysis.Fit\") — il contenitore da cui gli stadi di analisi leggono e in cui scrivono.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This step is the same whether the executor is pointed at a simulator or at a real device.\n"
msgstr "Questo passaggio è identico sia che l'executor punti a un simulatore sia a un dispositivo reale.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"analyze-the-data\" />\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "7. Analyze the data {#7-analyze-the-data}"
msgstr "7. Analizzare i dati {#7-analyze-the-data}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build an analysis pipeline around nonnegative least squares fitting of the model.\n"
msgstr "Costruisci una pipeline di analisi basata sul fitting del modello con i minimi quadrati non negativi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plot the measured observable means against their fitted exponentials, one subplot per `CZ` pair, to see whether the decays being fitted are exponential at all.\n"
msgstr "Traccia le medie delle osservabili misurate rispetto ai loro esponenziali di fit, un sottografico per ogni coppia `CZ`, per vedere se i decadimenti di cui si fa il fit sono davvero esponenziali.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Swap `exponential_fit` for `model_prediction` to compare the same data against the decays implied by the rates that came out of the non-negative least squares solve.\n"
msgstr "Sostituisci `exponential_fit` con `model_prediction` per confrontare gli stessi dati con i decadimenti implicati dai tassi ottenuti dalla soluzione dei minimi quadrati non negativi.\n"
